                                                "sense_id": "c9bc596f-c68e-34a0-ae61-dfd81c02b680",
                                                "text": "The plant will close and three-quarters of Britain's apple toffeeing capacity will lie idle."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "de411df1-8cc5-4232-bdbc-d8543061cfae",
                                                "sense_id": "c9bc596f-c68e-34a0-ae61-dfd81c02b680",
                                                "text": "But all the eating up of shoo-fly pie, and the cooking up of gauzy cumuli of pink candy, and the toffeeing of crab apples, couldn't hide the fact that we were winter-bound."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8c3f275e-c4be-4008-a2a3-6d5732958418",
                                                "sense_id": "c9bc596f-c68e-34a0-ae61-dfd81c02b680",
                                                "text": "The fire had claimed three of Mr. Barry's barns and the wine presses and the oak fermentation vessels were blackened and sprung, the wine-sugars toffeeing the floor."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
